# Phase 1 normalised every text file to LF on disk, but that only held for the
# machine that did it. A contributor with core.autocrlf=true would otherwise
# check out CRLF and commit it back, and the files most affected are the French
# ones, where a mixed line ending sits next to accented characters and makes a
# diff unreadable. Normalisation is therefore enforced in the repository rather
# than left to local Git configuration.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binaries. Declared explicitly so Git never attempts line ending conversion or
# text diffing on them. The decks are build outputs; the rule exists so that a
# deck committed under the branch-publishing fallback is not corrupted.
*.pptx binary
*.pdf binary
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
